# BUILD A COMPLETE BROWSER GAME: DEAD INTERNET

## YOUR ROLE

You are an expert indie game developer, senior frontend engineer, horror narrative designer, UI/UX designer, game systems programmer, and software tester.

Build a complete, playable browser game called DEAD INTERNET.

Do not just provide a design document, mockup, tutorial, or code snippets. Build the working application in the current project environment. Implement the actual game mechanics, interface, story, interactions, save system, audio controls, and endings.

Make sensible decisions independently. Do not stop to ask me questions. If a feature is too ambitious, implement a reliable smaller version rather than leaving a placeholder.

## 1. GAME OVERVIEW

Title: DEAD INTERNET

Tagline: EVERYONE ONLINE IS REAL. UNTIL THEY AREN'T.

Genre: Psychological horror, social deduction, mystery, interactive narrative, survival.

Platform: Desktop-first responsive web application, also usable on mobile browsers.

Audience: Players who enjoy internet mysteries, psychological horror, detective games, suspicious characters, moral decisions, branching stories, and unexpected plot twists.

The game takes place in the year 2041, after an unexplained event known as THE SILENCE.

Nearly every human communication network has collapsed. A mysterious surviving network called THE FEED continues to operate. Thousands of accounts remain online, posting messages and responding to one another.

Some accounts belong to real survivors.

Others are artificial entities that imitate human behaviour.

The player is a survivor operating a damaged computer terminal from an isolated underground shelter. Their objective is to identify trustworthy survivors, discover what caused THE SILENCE, and prevent the network from finding their physical location.

The central mystery: the network may be manipulating the player, and the player's own memories may not be trustworthy.

The game must have a complete beginning, middle, climax, and ending. The first playthrough should take approximately 20–35 minutes.

