## 5. THE PROLOGUE

The player awakens inside an underground shelter.

Their computer has restarted itself.

A damaged emergency broadcast says that all external communications are suspended.

The player discovers an anonymous message:

UNKNOWN USER — 03:17

"If you're reading this, don't trust the accounts that remember you."

The player has no memory of the previous six days.

The computer displays three surviving contacts:

1. MIRA — claims to be a medical student trapped in a hospital.
2. ELIAS — claims to be an engineer who helped build the network.
3. GHOST_17 — sends short, cryptic messages and refuses to provide personal information.

Each contact must have a unique writing style, personality, background, and hidden agenda.

The player can open their profiles, read their previous posts, and initiate conversations.

Introduce the central objective through an in-game system notification:

OBJECTIVE 01: IDENTIFY A TRUSTWORTHY SURVIVOR.

Secondary objective:

OBJECTIVE 02: DETERMINE WHY YOUR ACCOUNT WAS ACTIVE DURING THE SILENCE.

The player must be allowed to explore the interface before being forced to make a major decision.

